    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWith options `splitkeep=screen` and `showtabline=2`, opening a file location (far from the file start) in another window and later focusing on can change its cursor position.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a repro file with may lines, at least twice the available terminal lines. Let's say, the file contains at least 300 lines and is called `many-lines`.\n2. Create the following `init.lua`:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Set minimum set options to reproduce problematic behavior\n    vim.o.splitkeep = 'screen'\n    vim.o.showtabline = 2\n\n    -- Perform repro steps\n    vim.schedule(function()\n      -- Open another window. Can be either normal or floating window.\n      local target_win_id = vim.api.nvim_get_current_win()\n      vim.cmd('vertical split')\n\n      -- Open repro file in a normal target window\n      vim.api.nvim_win_set_buf(target_win_id, vim.fn.bufadd('many-lines'))\n\n      -- Set cursor to the line that is at least (around) two screen heights down\n      vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(target_win_id, { 300, 0 })\n\n      -- Immediately focus the target window. If done later by hand, doesn't repro.\n      vim.api.nvim_set_current_win(target_win_id)\n    end)\n    ```\n\n3. `nvim --clean -u init.lua`. Observe that the line focused in the target window is not 300, but a line with a number close to `vim.o.lines` (looks like `vim.o.lines - 3`).\n\nNotes:\n- Disabling either of set options makes this work as expected (the focused line is 300).\n- Not focusing on the target window has the correct target line. Focusing manually afterwards doesn't change cursor position.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCursor position never changes as a result of making the window current.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1115+g20a3bb3325\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNot sure, maybe\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.1.3-arch2-2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage",
