            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Minimal solution:\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/nvim/api/window.c b/src/nvim/api/window.c\nindex b1ffa0f6f2..2a1dd4a4aa 100644\n--- a/src/nvim/api/window.c\n+++ b/src/nvim/api/window.c\n@@ -126,6 +126,7 @@ void nvim_win_set_cursor(Window win, ArrayOf(Integer, 2) pos, Error *err)\n   w->w_cursor.lnum = (linenr_T)row;\n   w->w_cursor.col = (colnr_T)col;\n   w->w_cursor.coladd = 0;\n+  w->w_do_win_fix_cursor = false;\n   // When column is out of range silently correct it.\n   check_cursor_col(w);\n \n```\nHowever this also happens with:\n```vim\nfunc Split()\n  let win = win_getid()\n  vnew\n  call win_execute(win, 'call setline(1, range(1, 999))')\n  call win_execute(win, 'normal! 300gg')\n  call win_gotoid(win)\nendfunc\n\ncall feedkeys(\"\\<Cmd>call g:Split()\\<CR>\", 'n')\n```\nso it probably needs a better solution.",
